      "f23"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The delete, get, head, options, patch, post, and put functions send HTTP requests using their respective methods.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f14",
      "f15",
      "f16",
      "f17",
      "f18",
      "f19",
      "f20"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The request function sends an HTTP request with a configurable method.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f21"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The stream function is an alternative to request that streams the response body instead of loading it into memory at once.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f22"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "The create_ssl_context function creates an SSL context for verified connections.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f23"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Client and AsyncClient provide synchronous and asynchronous HTTP clients with connection pooling, HTTP/2, redirects, and cookie persistence.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f25",
      "f28"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "ASGITransport and WSGITransport are custom transports for sending requests directly to ASGI and WSGI applications respectively.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f24",
      "f38"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "AsyncHTTPTransport, BaseTransport, and AsyncBaseTransport are transport base classes for custom connection handling.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f39",
      "f41",
      "f42"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Auth is the base class for authentication schemes, with BasicAuth for HTTP Basic authentication, FunctionAuth for callable authentication, and NetRCAuth for netrc file credentials.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f26",
      "f27",
      "f31",
      "f34"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Headers provides case-insensitive multi-dict HTTP headers, Cookies provides mutable mapping HTTP cookies, and QueryParams provides multi-dict URL query parameters.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f30",
      "f32",
      "f35"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "URL breaks down URL components.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f37"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Timeout configures timeout behavior and Limits configures limits on client behaviors.",
     "fact_ids": [
      "f33",
      "f36"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "codes provides HTTP status codes and reason phrases.",
     "fact_ids": [
